Local.xcconfig

# Internal documents — deliberately NOT published (decided 2026-08-09).
#
# The test applied to every document in this repository: name the reader, and name
# what that reader can decide after reading it. The ones that ship pass it —
# README (use it), SECURITY (grant it permissions), CONTRIBUTING (send a patch),
# SELECTION-LAYER (change the ranker), MAP-ARCHITECTURE (change the data model).
# The ones below do not. They are the author's own working record, and a public
# reader can decide nothing with them:
#
#   STRATEGY / MARKET      the commercial plan and the competitor revenue ledger
#   ROADMAP                a route to publication, which publication ends
#   DESIGN / -NORTHSTAR    the visual direction, frozen — nothing here to govern
#   INTERNAL-*.md          chapters lifted out of CLAUDE / DIRECTION / HARNESS
#
# None of this is deleted. The files stay on disk and stay authoritative for the
# person writing them; they are simply not part of the published surface.
# Documents that ship reference them in plain text, never as links, so nothing
# dangles in the published tree.
STRATEGY-2026-08.md
MARKET-2026-08.md
ROADMAP.md
DESIGN.md
DESIGN-NORTHSTAR.md
INTERNAL-*.md

# Build artifacts that land in the repo root
default.profraw

# Real-log eval cases (eval/real/harvest.sh). These are windows cut straight out
# of a live mull DB — raw keystrokes, clipboard, window titles — so the harness
# ships and the corpus never does. The whole point of the real harness is that
# each person runs it against their OWN log.
eval/real/cases/*.json
